From 038c6132c01570642b6a43a68add3ecf70d62091 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 17:24:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(auth): derive the OIDC cookie metaclass from the
 installed State metaclass

`OIDCCookieMeta` subclassed `reflex.vars.BaseStateMeta` directly. reflex
0.9.12 (reflex-dev/reflex#7136) moved `rx.State` onto `_StateMeta`, a
*sibling* subclass of `BaseStateMeta`, so `OIDCCookieMeta` is no longer a
subclass of the metaclass of `OIDCAuthState`'s bases and

    class OIDCAuthState(ConfigMixin, rx.State, mixin=True, metaclass=OIDCCookieMeta)

raises `TypeError: metaclass conflict` at import. That kills every app
configuring `AuthPlugin`, `MCPPlugin` or `EventHandlerAPIPlugin` at startup
(the plugin's post_compile reaches `auth/enforcement.py`, which imports this
module), including apps that configure no auth at all.

Read the metaclass off the installed reflex instead -- `type(rx.State)` is
`BaseStateMeta` up to 0.9.11 and `_StateMeta` from 0.9.12, so the one
declaration works on both. Under a type checker the alias stays
`BaseStateMeta`, keeping the `__new__` override checked. The cookie
descriptors the metaclass stamps on a provider state are unchanged.

reflex may also fix this on its side (reflex-dev/reflex#7211), but
reflex-enterprise must not depend on that: 0.9.5 is published with
`reflex[db] >=0.9.6` and no upper bound.

Refs reflex-dev/reflex#7211

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NeyxWsuC9hqSKq8YcEwZyY
